## What to deliver

Build and rig the hatchery up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a squat, wide hive-mound clustered with hatch
cells (the fixed root), a central iris hatch on the crown, and a vent set into the
side. The required interface is two auto joints — **`hatch_turn`** that turns the
iris hatch about its vertical axis and **`vent_bob`** that lifts the vent up and
settles it back — each on its own looping clip, while the `base` stays fixed.
Produce **every** required part and joint; you may add your own extra parts,
joints, or auto-play clips on top, but do not drop or contradict the required
interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json`
are your finished submission.
